From 71e3be4f114f0a2810398cf46c799c6d614375ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:05:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(fog): transport resolved native fog settings

Retain complete PLAYER_FOG snapshots and resolve command, biome and
existing registry-default settings against the connection-selected packs.
Publish one immutable version-2 snapshot after join and channel negotiation,
including empty command resets and late registrations. Preserve distance
units and colors without inferring field-level inheritance.

Native Bedrock 1.26.60.5 with BDS 1.26.60.6 (protocol 2225) confirms
unsigned-count string-array snapshots, topmost matching-medium precedence,
and water-only fallback to lower air settings. A qualified End-biome fixture
renders red fog from 0 to 32 blocks without commands or living dragons.
Both prior Java routes read the red registry color but kept 1,024 blocks.

Empty command stacks now retain world resources. World replacement retires
the entire snapshot, and payload decoding rejects ambiguous biome aliases
and unsupported versions. Regressions cover medium precedence, immutable
resource ownership, codec bounds, late registration, command removal and
world replacement. Biome-boundary blending, legacy data-default bindings,
and native engine-specific vanilla rules remain separate acceptance work.

BREAKING CHANGE: FogDefinition includes distances; FogState requires biome/default settings and the negotiated fog payload uses version 2.
